title: 'Consequence: a replaced root keeps the containers folder of the node it replaced.'
pid: e7b8e4fd-3a44-4a48-a6a4-8865b53e4d47
body: |2-
  A fresh view draws the root's containers folder once, at opening.
  After the root is re-pointed, the folder still lists what contains
  the original, each drawn noWarrant, since nothing relates them to the
  override. Switching back makes them warranted again. Clearing the
  folder would lose it for the way back. Left so; Jeff may mind.
